-## 3. Findings
+## 3. Does the chart now show where pay concentrates? (viz-even, measured)
+
+Clusters, default view (Group by department), every board, from the drawn circles and each row's postings
+(scratchpad `clusters.mjs`, `even.mjs`). "Before" is viz-even's own measurement of the old chart on the same crawl.
+A "band" is one exact midpoint carried by at least 3 postings and 5% of its row (viz-even's "mode").
+
+| Board, width | Circles before → now | Bands sharing a circle before → now | Gap CV now (before: 0) | Circles at the 9 px floor |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Amazon 1440 | 44 → 70 | 22 → 19 of 30 | 0.22 | 44 of 70 |
+| Amazon 390 | 44 → 61 | 22 → 21 of 30 | 0.22 | 45 of 61 |
+| Apple 1440 | 41 → 60 | 26 → 27 of 36 | 0.27 | 47 of 60 |
+| Google 1440 | 46 → 65 | 15 → 6 of 29 | 0.24 | 34 of 65 |
+| Meta 1440 | 38 → 60 | 32 of 41 → 28 of 44 | 0.21 | 31 of 60 |
+| Microsoft 1440 | 51 → 47 | 8 → 10 of 32 | 0.26 | 33 of 47 |
+| Microsoft 390 | 30 → 45 | 24 → 11 of 32 | 0.26 | 33 of 45 |
+| NVIDIA 1440 | 44 → 39 | 24 → 31 of 38 | 0.25 | 20 of 39 |
+| Netflix 1440 | 38 → 38 | 9 → 10 of 19 | 0.33 | 16 of 38 |
+| Anduril 1440 | 34 → 51 | 22 → 11 of 33 | 0.24 | 45 of 51 |
+
+(Meta's band count includes near-twins such as $151.496K and $151.5K, so its "sharing" is overstated.)
+
+Verdict:
+- **Positions are now honest.** Every circle sits at its postings' median midpoint: 0 px off on every board,
+  except near the plot's ends, where a circle is held inside the plot (Apple Marketing's $349K circle, 8.2 px).
+  Before: 6–14 px on average, 34 px at most. Circles add up to the salaried count on all 8 boards.
+- **The lattice is gone.** Neighbouring gaps now vary with the data (CV 0.19–0.33, against exactly one bin
+  width before). Google's Software Engineering row has its own circle for each posted band ($179K, $213K, $254K,
+  $313K). Google, Microsoft (phone) and Anduril keep their bands apart far better.
+- **What still looks even, for reasons of drawing:**
+  - *Size* (V-34). 42–92% of circles are drawn at the 9 px floor. On Amazon a floor circle holds anything from
+    1 to 123 postings. So most rows read as strings of identical dots with one or two bigger ones.
+  - *Spacing where pay is a continuum.* Amazon's per-place ranges make hundreds of distinct midpoints (Project/
+    Program/Product Management–Technical: 95; the "30 more departments" row: 1,034). The merge rule tiles that
+    continuum at 1.1–1.8× the touch spacing. P/P/PM–Technical's nine circles sit 28–41 px apart (CV 0.11; 0.08 on
+    a phone), and 6 of its 8 neighbouring pairs have less than $10K of empty pay between them. That spacing is
+    the merge threshold, not the data; only the sizes could show the concentration there, and V-34 flattens them.
+  - *Merging.* On Amazon desktop the plan does not settle and merges two real peaks (V-33). On NVIDIA (0.8 px per
+    $1K, an axis to $500K) bands $16–24K apart are 13–19 px apart, closer than two circles can be. So 31 of 38
+    bands share a circle, more than the old $50K bins (24). Example: "141 roles, midpoints $183K–$236K · median
+    $220K" holds $196.75K ×28, $219.75K ×70 and $235.75K ×35. The tooltip gives the spread, but the drawing
+    hides it. A per-row strip of tick marks, or letting circles overlap, would show it.
+- **Ranges.** Stacking removes the rows of identical bars: Amazon's 13,980 bars become 2,256 rows (6.2 per row;
+  Apple 6.6, Anduril 6.9, Netflix 2.1). But the height now follows distinct ranges, not postings (V-38), so the
+  bars spread evenly down the chart wherever the postings are. The distribution strip above the chart is now the
+  only drawing of where postings concentrate.
+
